 "id": "14e8dca3-ef35-46b2-9b5a-00ed081e8af9",
 "type": "manga",
 "attributes": {
  "title": {
   "en": "Picture Bride: Umi wo Watatte Koi to Nare"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja": "ピクチャーブライド　～海を渡って恋となれ～"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "San Francisco, early 20th century. Relying on a single photograph, some women crossed the ocean to marry husbands they had never met. Chizuru, who works as a teacher, is one of them. Her husband, Yoshiaki, lives in a free and equal society, with progressive ideas, and respects her. Chizuru had high hopes for a life married to him, but when she met Yoshiaki in America, he was a completely different person to the one in the photograph... A love story that begins with marriage, where the two grow to love each other despite their differences in a place far from their homeland.\n\n(Source: Comic Walker, translated)",
   "ja": "２０世紀初頭、サンフランシスコ。写真１枚を頼りに海を渡り、まだ見ぬ夫のもとへ嫁いだ女性たちがいた。\n教師として働く千鶴もその一人。\n自由で平等な社会、先進的な思想、そして千鶴を尊重してくれる夫・義昭。彼との結婚生活に期待を抱いていた千鶴だったが、米国の地で対面した義昭は写真とはまったく異なる人物で……\n故郷からはるか遠く離れた地で反発しあいながらも愛情を深めていく、結婚から始まる恋物語。"
  },
